<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Randgold details Mali Syama gold operation.</title>
<headline>Randgold details Mali Syama gold operation.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Randgold Resources, the African gold mining and exploration arm of South Africa's Randgold and Exploration Co Ltd, on Thursday published an operating summary for its Syama gold mine in Mali.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p>			    Quarter ended		 Forecast for</p>
<p>			    March 31, 1997		quarter ending</p>
<p>								June 30, 1997</p>
<p>Tonnes mined	    3.45 million			4.3 million</p>
<p>Tonnes milled	   0.28 million			0.28 million</p>
<p>Ounces produced	 35,312			  40,500</p>
<p>Average price</p>
<p>     received	   $350/ounce		    $350/ounce</p>
<p>Cash operating</p>
<p>	   costs	  $330/ounce		    $305/ounce</p>
<p>Cash operating</p>
<p>   profit/loss	  $114,000 loss		 $900,000 profit</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
